# Compiled binaries — every module builds to its own folder name by default,
# so there is no single pattern that catches them. These are the ones this
# repo produces.
bin/
dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# `go build ./cmd/api` with no -o writes a binary named after the package into the
# working directory. There is no pattern that catches every such name, so the ones
# this repo produces are listed.
/backends/learning/docker-concepts/api

# `go build` inside a lesson folder writes a binary named after the folder, and
# one (go-concepts/06-goroutines/06-goroutines, 2.6 MB) was committed before this
# line existed. A file inside a numbered lesson folder with the folder's own
# number-and-name shape is always that binary; no source file is named that way.
/go-concepts/[0-9][0-9]-*/[0-9][0-9]-*
!/go-concepts/[0-9][0-9]-*/[0-9][0-9]-*/

# Go build and module caches live outside the repo, but `go work vendor`
# and `go mod vendor` write here.
vendor/

# Coverage and profiling artifacts
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
cpu.pprof
mem.pprof

# Generated code IS committed, deliberately, and this is where the reasoning lives
# because it is the kind of decision that gets reversed by whoever touches the
# file next.
#
# The rule for a private service with a build pipeline is "regenerate, do not
# commit": the generator runs in CI, the tree stays small, and a stale checked-in
# file cannot drift from its source.
#
# The rule for a repo someone CLONES is the opposite, and this is one of those.
# `git clone && go build ./...` has to work with nothing but a Go toolchain. With
# the stubs ignored it needs protoc, protoc-gen-go, protoc-gen-go-grpc and a
# matching gqlgen, which is four installs and four versions to agree on before
# the first line compiles. That is the difference between a repo you can read and
# a repo you have to set up.
#
# It is also the Go community's convention: the standard library commits its
# generated files, and every gRPC project on pkg.go.dev ships its .pb.go, because
# `go get` runs no generators.
#
# So: the stubs are committed, each generator has a script next to it, and the
# check that they have not drifted is a CI step that regenerates and diffs rather
# than a .gitignore entry.
#
#   gRPC stubs:   backends/learning/grpc-concepts/generate.sh
#   gqlgen:       `go run github.com/99designs/gqlgen generate` in graphql-concepts

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.history/

# A working plan kept at the root while a multi-step change is in progress.
# It is scratch, never committed; LESSONS.md is the part that stays.
PLAN.md

# Version stamps from the makefile-concepts example workflow.
.tools/
